      'Setup example: 10 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Collect the most complete quartets (sets of four matching cards) by asking other players for specific cards.',
      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Turn**: The player whose turn it is asks any other player for a specific card (e.g. 'Do you have the King of Hearts?'). 2. **Requirement**: The asker must hold at least one card of the same quartet. 3. **If the asked player has it**: They must give it; the asker gets another turn and may ask again. 4. **If not**: The asked player says 'Not at home' (Nicht da); the turn passes to them. (2-player: the asked player draws one card from the stock before asking.) 5. **Quartets**: When a player completes a quartet, they place it face-up (or face-down) on the table. 6. **End**: Play continues until all cards are in quartets. The player with the most quartets wins.",
      'Scoring example: One point per quartet collected. Winner is the player with the most quartets when all cards are laid down. The player with the most complete quartets at the end wins. Ties possible..',
